    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0235" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg117"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Chang Yen Soon to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1889-01-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3, 1889</date>. (Received
                        January 4.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that since I
                    wrote to apprise you of my having, in accordance with the precedent of the Rock
                    Springs case, memorialized the throne for an Imperial decree in connection with
                    the amount of $276,619.75 indemnity for losses and injuries sustained by Chinese
                    in this country, I have this day received, by telegraph, the Imperial decree
                    authorizing me to receive the same for distribution amongst them.</p>
                <p>I would therefore deem it a favor if you will kindly name a day for me to receive
                    the payment.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chang Yen Hoon</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
